==Battleground==
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 43.33~50 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,500f</sup>.
*2 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>, delay 76.67 seconds<sup>2,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 76.67 seconds<sup>2,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 76.67 seconds<sup>2,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Queen B]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is not very different from [[Royal Jelly Hell (Merciless)|Royal Jelly Hell]], relying on extremely strong but limited nasty peons for pressure, particularly Lutrinae Gokurakko. For this reason, you should include a bit of variety for your units and prioritize on defeating Lutrinae Gokurakko. Once they're gone, Queen B is not much of a threat and can be taken down easily.

Alternatively, on 1 Crown, Queen B can be rushed and defeated before the first Goku Otter arrives by a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], removing much of the challenge from this stage.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: Stone's Immunity to Knockback and Slow, alongside its extreme health, makes it an excellent supportive meatshield. It can easily invade Queen B's blindspot with its speed, and pin the Otters for your attackers to defeat them.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier is fast and deals massive damage to Reds, which might be just what's needed to swiftly eliminate the Jackrabbits when paired with fast meatshields to ensure they cannot get inside Courier's blindspot.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]]: Lasvoss is Immune to Slow and Knockback, so timing is not required to get him inside Queen B's blindspot and Goruakko's knockback can't displace him. Lasvoss' main appeal however lies in his already high base damage, savage blow and 50% strengthen at 30% health, which combined with his 320 range can be enough to wipe out a whole wave of Otter variants. Notably, at level 50, he does just about the damage a 250% Gokurakko could absorb with a strengthened Savage blow. His survive ability and range advantage further increases his chances of success, although you might require several resets before he lands the important attack.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: with his Slow Resist Talent unlocked, he can easily get into Queen B's blindspot and do big damage to supports. Even without the Talent, proper timing, and/or some help from Curseblast/Thunderbolt can help him get in.
*[[One-Eyed Asuka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blue Eyed Asuka]]: she Immune to Slow, and because of this, she can easily get into her blindspot at Lv.40. With her Curse, she can be a huge help for non-Slow-Immune units trying to enter the blindspot. Just be sure to time said units for while Queen B is Cursed, as the uptime is only around 50%.

